{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-26T20:51:00.723Z","data":{"text":"Task complete.\n\n**Summary**\n\nImplemented the stacked cut/halt watcher step:\n\n- **`src/core/spec/stack-cut.ts`** (new) — `decideStackCut` returns wait / halt (`dependency_changed`, `dependency_diverged`) / cut with a base, reading `.run/stacked-on` and dependency state via `stack-dependencies.ts`; `cutStackedChange` creates the branch/worktree, runs `runPrepare`, seals the stacked copy with an `osq: <id> approved` commit and `.run/base`, deletes the stacked approval, and returns the worktree path.\n- **`src/watcher/stack-run.ts`** (new) — `runStackedChanges` visits stacked changes in order, skips regressed ones, cuts/halts, logs each cut, and halts `stack_cut_failed` on error.\n- **`src/watcher/worktree-run.ts`** — `WorktreeHaltReason` gains the three new reasons.\n- **`src/watcher/loop.ts`** — `runWatcherCycle` calls `runStackedChanges` once before listing changes.\n- **`tests/stack-run.test.ts`** (new) — all 6 \"Stacked cut\" and 3 \"Stacked halt\" scenarios (9/9 pass).\n\n`node --import tsx --test tests/stack-run.test.ts` passes 9/9, and the proposal verify `pnpm verify` (typechecks, build, full suite, lint) passes.\n\nOne documented deviation: a failed cut removes the worktree it added (keeping the branch and stacked approval) because `changeTrees` hides a stacked tree behind any `osq/<folder>` worktree, so `retrySpec`/the next cycle could not otherwise find the change. This is recorded in `openspec/changes/094-stacking/.run/results/4.md`."}}
